A||||15||FieroFanaticus2||Custom FireWall (Behind the seats) Idea||||1||
Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||11-15-2001||05:09 PM||||I took the firewall out of my parts car and thought I would wrap it in black vinyl and see how it looks.  I took some pics of the process and thought I would share them with all of you.<P>Here's the firewall, with the furry stuff removed.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150004.JPG"> <P>Then the firewall upside down glueing to the vinyl.  I used industrial strength spray adhesive and covered the firewall with it, then layed it down on a flat sheet of vinyl.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150006.JPG"> <P>Around the spot where the ECM sits I used a hairdrier to heat the vinyl up enough to be able to stretch it, then used heavy duty staples to hold it in place.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150017.JPG"> <P>After trimming the excess Vinyl off, I taped up the padding, and folded over the vinyl to cover the edges.  I used 409 glue to tack it into place, but any strong quick drying glue should work fine.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150020.JPG"> <P>And after about 2 1/2 hours it's finished.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150022.JPG"> <P>Total cost = about $4.00 for the vinyl.  And a few cents for the glue used.<P>I think it looks pretty nice and would look even better with a couple of Mr. Mike's Leather seats sitting in front of it.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||11-15-2001||05:17 PM||||WELL DONE! You may want to accent that with padded vinyl on the door bottoms in place of the carpet like DXR_DAD.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||11-15-2001||05:18 PM||||Nice customization... can't wait to see it in your car with your seats!  It'll look great.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-15-2001||07:10 PM||||That's exactly what I did (both the vinyl covered firewall cover and the lower door panels).  Good job.  Mine looks just like that (but really, really dusty).  I'm going to do something totally different with the firewall/interior so mine now sits in the (unused) dining room collecting dust.  ::sigh::  Oh, well.  Another project turned to scrap.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||11-15-2001||08:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B>WELL DONE! You may want to accent that with padded vinyl on the door bottoms in place of the carpet like DXR_DAD.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That exactly what I plan on doing.  I'm in the process of adding power windows and locks to my car anyway, so might as well while the doors are apart.  I'm thinking I'll do it to the headliner as well since I'm swapping out the front clip for one with a factory sunroof.  I'll be buying the leather seats this winter, as well as new carpet too.  I'm hoping that I'll be able to finish it all by the Dells Run this coming spring, but it's starting to look kind of shady on that --  Still have the hoodscoops that need to be sealed and the hood repainted, and the side scoops to be sealed, fit, and painted, as well as install a scoop on the rear decklid.  I have a problem of starting new projects before I complete old ones.  My head is about to spin off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||72vinman||11-15-2001||10:34 PM||||Great Job. That is very similar to what I have done. My Firewall is black tight weave carpet which matches the lower panels of the door. The top panels of the door are black leather. I am also having the center console covered in the same leather.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigvin2_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||11-15-2001||10:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroFanaticus2:<BR><B>I took the firewall out of my parts car and thought I would wrap it in black vinyl and see how it looks.  I took some pics of the process and thought I would share them with all of you.<P>Here's the firewall, with the furry stuff removed.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150004.JPG">  <P>Then the firewall upside down glueing to the vinyl.  I used industrial strength spray adhesive and covered the firewall with it, then layed it down on a flat sheet of vinyl.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150006.JPG">  <P>Around the spot where the ECM sits I used a hairdrier to heat the vinyl up enough to be able to stretch it, then used heavy duty staples to hold it in place.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150017.JPG">  <P>After trimming the excess Vinyl off, I taped up the padding, and folded over the vinyl to cover the edges.  I used 409 glue to tack it into place, but any strong quick drying glue should work fine.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150020.JPG">  <P>And after about 2 1/2 hours it's finished.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB150022.JPG">  <P>Total cost = about $4.00 for the vinyl.  And a few cents for the glue used.<P>I think it looks pretty nice and would look even better with a couple of Mr. Mike's Leather seats sitting in front of it.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>WOW.. Looks Great. Ever think about..... Oh lets say.. Makeing one to sell? (Hint-Hint)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">   <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
