Z||000012||Mr.Frosty||11-18-2001||01:16 AM||||It's pretty easy to remove.If you consider removing the center console,and B-pillars easy ,then Yes it's easy.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jncomutt||11-18-2001||01:18 AM||||I used the 3M stuff.  It works great in my opinion, no problems yet.<P>And yes, it does come off very easy.  You do have to remove the center console, for there are 3 phillips screws that need to come off.  The Rest just attaches using those push/pin type clips.  Just unscrew, give a quick tug and its out.  <P>EDIT:<P>     WOO - HOOOOO!!!!!   300 posts!!!! hehe<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 11-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Smoooooth GT||11-18-2001||10:59 AM||||3 screw's?? that's it!! hmm.. Great something else to dive into...lol Thank's for the information!!  Steve<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/texas_1.gif">          <BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000015||FieroFanaticus2||11-18-2001||12:22 PM||||The Spray adhesive I used is;<P>Camie<BR>363<BR>High Strength<BR>Fast Tack<BR>spray adhesive<P>Fast Tack<BR>Lace Spray Pattern<BR>Pressure sensitive<P>says ' For Industrial Use Only '<P>I 'borrowed' a can of it from the place I work, which they use it in the R&D department as a bonder when experimenting.<P>There is no web address on the can, but there is a physical address as well as a phone number.<P>Camie - Campbell, INC<BR>9225 Watson Industrial Park<BR>St. Louis, MO  63126<BR>1-800-325-9572<P>I looked this stuff up on my work's inventory list, says it's about $18.00 a can (24 Fl. OZ).  They buy it by the carton.<P>Don't get it between your fingers either.||||reg||1
